<H3><CENTER><FONT COLOR="#ffff00"><A HREF="mailto:O-Zwei@t-online.de">Oliver Okon</A></FONT></CENTER></H3>

Oliver has a red 1991 Sedicivalvole with 108,000 Km. The car is
really going like hell, as it reaches 7000 rpm. It would go further except for the
rev limiter. In 5th gear on a nearly straight motorways it showned an indicated
235 Km/h. Unfortunately the faster the car is going the more oil it drinks. Oliver's
car is consuming about 2 litres every 1000 km.
<P>
He really likes the car, because in his eyes it is a underdog.
If it was not for the sake of the engine, he really would like to see
how far the revs would go. It really did not seem to want to stop at
7000 rpm.
<P>
Changes made so far:
<UL>
<LI>MOMO steering wheel - 30 cm Top Power.</LI>
<LI>MOMO Gear Knob and red gaiter.</LI>
<LI>CMS alloys 7*15 with 195/50 15 Bridgestone B 530</LI>
<LI>Red side indicators from the VW Golf II</LI>
<LI>K&amp;N filtercharger, as the 57i Kit is far too loud for the city.</LI>
</UL>

